+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] windows.gaming.input: Register the ArcadeStick and FlightStick
+ runtime classes.
+
+A title that looks for an arcade stick or a flight stick through Windows.Gaming.Input asks RoGetActivationFactory for Windows.Gaming.Input.ArcadeStick or .FlightStick; the dll never registered either class, so the call returned REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG and the title's controller setup gave up before it reached the pad it would actually have used. The two classes now have a custom game controller factory each, built from the same stubs as RacingWheel, so the factory resolves and the collection comes back empty instead of failing. The mutable IVector the backing store needs was the one parametrized collection the idl had left out for both.
